  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Question": "The diagonal \\(AC\\) of square \\(ABCD\\) has length 8. Find the area of the square.",
  "Choices": {},
  "Correct Answer": "32",
  "Accepted Answers": [],
  "Unordered Answers": false,
  "Solution": "The area of a square equals half the product of its diagonals: \\(8\\times8\\div2=32\\).\n\nAlternative method 1: Find the side length squared\n\nLet \\(s>0\\) be the side length of the square. Diagonal \\(AC\\) is the hypotenuse of a right triangle with two legs of length \\(s\\), so the Pythagorean theorem gives\n\\[\n2s^2=8^2,\\qquad s^2=32.\n\\]\nThe square's area is \\(s^2\\), so its area is \\(32\\).",
